Step 1: Check for Existing pip Installation
1. Run the command to check if pip is already installed: sudo rpm -qa | grep pip

Step 2: Download pip Installation Package
1. Download the pip installation package using wget: wget https://dl.fedoraproject.org/pub/archive/epel/7/x86_64/Packages/p/python2-pip-8.1.2-14.el7.noarch.rpm

Step 3: Install pip
1. Install pip using yum localinstall: sudo yum localinstall python2-pip-8.1.2-14.el7.noarch.rpm

Step 4: Verify pip Installation
1. Verify pip installation by listing installed packages: sudo pip2.7 list

Step 5: Install pymongo
1. Install pymongo using pip: sudo pip2.7 install pymongo==3.8.0
2. Alternative command (if above command fails): sudo pip2.7 install --trusted-host pypi.org --trusted-host pypi.python.org --trusted-host files.pythonhosted.org pymongo==3.8.0
